  "note": "Store brands a Strongsville food bank receives that Walmart does not sell, and the GS1 company prefixes their barcodes start with (the 7 leading digits of the 13-digit form, measured on Open Facts 2026-10-19). One file for the pipeline (crawler/identify.py: a listed brand is matched to Walmart's own brands, the same price tier) and the app (the pack manifest: a typed brand name ranks Walmart's own-brand items first and the sheet says why; a scanned barcode under a listed prefix is named by its store even when nothing else is known about it). Brand names are matched whole, case-insensitively, apostrophes aside. Add a store or brand here; the next pack build and identify refresh pick it up. A brand that is also an ordinary word or a brand Walmart sells (Presto cookware, Boulder Canyon chips, Beneful Healthy Radiance, Summit, Elevation, Belmont, Brookdale, Stonemill Kitchens) is left out on purpose: in a typed query it would be taken for the store brand (measured 2026-10-19). Member's Mark is Walmart-owned (Sam's Club) and Walmart.com sells it, so it is a Walmart store brand (crawler/normalize.py STORE_BRANDS), not listed here. `owners`: words of the chain's company name as USDA FoodData Central lists the brand owner (crawler/identify.py keeps the branded foods of these owners, their listed brands and their barcode prefixes).",
